","is_correct":false}],"explanation":"Mandarin has nearly a billion native speakers, more than any other language."},{"id":"q7","question":"How many days are there in a leap year?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"364","is_correct":false},{"id":"b","text":"365","is_correct":false},{"id":"c","text":"366","is_correct":true},{"id":"d","text":"367","is_correct":false}],"explanation":"A leap year adds 29 February to keep the calendar aligned with Earth''s orbit."},{"id":"q8","question":"In which country did the Olympic Games originate?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Italy","is_correct":false},{"id":"b","text":"Greece","is_correct":true},{"id":"c","text":"Egypt","is_correct":false},{"id":"d","text":"France","is_correct":false}],"explanation":"The ancient Games were held at Olympia from 776 BC."}]'::jsonb,
