","is_correct":false}],"explanation":"Athena emerged in armour and became goddess of wisdom and strategic warfare."},{"id":"q7","question":"Who flew too close to the Sun on wings of feathers and wax?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Icarus","is_correct":true},{"id":"b","text":"Daedalus","is_correct":false},{"id":"c","text":"Orpheus","is_correct":false},{"id":"d","text":"Bellerophon","is_correct":false}],"explanation":"Icarus ignored his father Daedalus''s warning and fell into the sea."},{"id":"q8","question":"Which creature, half man and half bull, lived in the Labyrinth of Crete?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Centaur","is_correct":false},{"id":"b","text":"Minotaur","is_correct":true},{"id":"c","text":"Cyclops","is_correct":false},{"id":"d","text":"Satyr","is_correct":false}],"explanation":"The Minotaur was eventually slain by the Athenian hero Theseus."}]'::jsonb,
